  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The natural frequency of an oscillating system is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"f_{0}\"></span>. An external applied force acts on the system with frequency <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"f_{D}\"></span>. The oscillations are heavily damped. </p>\n<p>What is true about the relationship between <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"f_{0}\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"f_{D}\"></span> when the amplitude of the oscillations is a maximum?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"f_{0} = f_{D}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"f_{0} &lt; f_{D}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"f_{0} &gt; f_{D}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\">The relationship cannot be determined from the given information. </li>\n</ol>"
  },
